Step 4 (Wave A): 8 structural agents (01-08), all Opus tier

shared/schemas.ts expanded with Zod runtime schemas for all 44 agents
(Wave 0 + 40 specialists across A/B/C/D). Mirrors src/types/agents.ts
TypeScript interfaces, with z.literal pinning agent_id per agent.

Wave A specialists — base composite owners + structural readers:

agent-01 Prior Trend Strength (Opus, 600 tokens)
- 8-state taxonomy: strong_young / strong_mature / healthy_ongoing /
  trend_forming / weak_decaying / chop_disguised / no_trend /
  parabolic_exhaustion. 5-signature parabolic catalogue caps score at 50.
- Variant B regime-establishment routes to trend_forming (45-59).

agent-02 EMA Cloud Geometry (Opus, 700 tokens)
- HEAVIEST base composite contributor — 39 percent of Wave E score
  (cloud compression 25 + EMA acceleration 14 via 70/30 split).
- Per-pair slope numeric estimates for blue/yellow/white plus regime_label
  from 13-category visual library. Macro_visible flag handles TOS mobile
  cropping. Direction-bias-via-weighted-slope-sum.

agent-03 Pullback Geometry (Opus, 600 tokens)
- Variant A only; abstains on B/C/D. 6-signature shape taxonomy.
- depth_tier_multiplier (0.50-1.05) consumed by Wave E for tier interaction.
- through_macro forces abstain (structural break).

agent-04 Cloud Penetration (Opus, 700 tokens)
- Routing label tier (1/2/3/null) drives downstream tier-specific rubrics.
- 6 penetration classes, 5-band residence-time tier-downgrade logic.
- Wick:body ratio with >=2.0 = gold. Multi-touch tracking with
  +5/+10/-10 score adjustments. tier_provisional flag for sparse
  Tier 3 corpus evidence.

agent-05 Market Structure HH/HL or LH/LL (Opus, 600 tokens)
- Pivots are primary, EMAs derived. 6-state intactness taxonomy.
- Magnitude filter at 1x blue cloud width. EMA-vs-structure conflict
  resolution rules. Range mode for non-trending charts.

agent-06 Trend Maturity Exhaustion (Opus, 600 tokens)
- Score INVERTS with maturity (higher = more mature). 7-state taxonomy
  with established (41-60) as the entry sweet spot.
- 5-signature visual catalogue; >=2 firing forces actively_exhausting.
- consider_reversal=true at actively_exhausting/blow_off.
- Naive sum with Agent 11 forbidden per Wave E spec section 5
  (multiplicative interaction).

agent-07 Choppiness Regime (Opus, 700 tokens, VETO YES)
- 7 regime labels. Veto fires on label=CHOP AND confidence>=75 AND
  not abstain. Sub-30s timeframes escalate to 85.
- veto_overridable flag for soft-chop/HTF-context/event-window cases.
- Cost-asymmetry argument: false-pass is 3-4x worse than false-veto.
- Right-edge weighting 2x for transition-from-chop charts.
- News interaction: Agent 22 event-window flag down-weights chop reading.

agent-08 Multi-EMA Confluence (Opus, 600 tokens)
- ALIGNMENT-GATE OWNER. alignment_against drives Wave E hard cap:
  none -> no cap; short_structural OR macro -> cap 55;
  both_macro_and_short_structural -> cap 40; all_tangled -> cap 50
  with verdict-mode downgrade.
- tier_backdrop (0/1/2/3) decoupled from Agent 04 tier (which-cloud-
  touched vs regime-quality-supporting).
- Which-two-of-three logic: blue dissent forgivable, macro dissent
  most concerning.

Tests: 46 new tests across 8 agents covering happy paths, all enum
values, schema validation failures, abstain handling, tier-specific
behavior. Verifies Opus model selection and per-agent max_tokens.

167 vitest passing total (121 from Step 3 + 46 new). 134 pytest still
passing. TypeScript type-check clean.
